  "provenance": "Markers compiled from publicly published advisories: I4C citizen advisory on digital arrest, PhonePe Trust & Safety, Seqrite threat research, RBI advisories on remote-access-app fraud, and mainstream red-flag explainers. No private or field data.",
  "notes": "Romanised (Hinglish) spellings are included deliberately so keyword matching survives imperfect ASR on code-switched speech. Match case-insensitively on a normalised transcript. 1.2.0 brings the Devanagari half to parity with the Latin half: the hi-IN recogniser emits Devanagari, and with only 16 markers in that script a Hindi-transcribed call was matched against a seventh of the lexicon. Negative guards were transliterated in the same pass — guards are the false-positive defence, and a Latin-only guard set would have raised the score on exactly the legitimate Hindi calls it exists to protect.",
